title: hello panel
tags: Panel [[Writing a panel type]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
aliases: hello example example-panel
summary: The smallest panel type: it shows its workspace and the active repository, and registers one command — a directory to copy to start a panel of your own.

`hello` is an example, not a tool: two files, about forty lines, to copy under
`~/.config/metafolder/gui/panel-types/<your-name>/` ([[Writing a panel type]]).
Show it with `panel:open here hello`.

It does one thing of each kind a panel does:

* it finds its elements in its root — `byId(root, 'workspace')`, from `/__ui.js`;
* it reads a workspace variable, `active_repo`, and follows it with `workspace.onChange`. A variable is `unknown` to the type checker, so the panel says how it becomes text;
* it registers a command, [[hello:greet]], which writes to the status bar.

It reads nothing from the daemon, so it has nothing to defer and no change feed to
follow; `mount` returns nothing because nothing is attached outside the root
([[The metafolder API]]).
